Description: schematic editor and circuit simulator built with Qt6
 Circuit Master is a cross-platform schematic editor and
 circuit simulator written in C++17 with Qt6.
 .
 It provides a grid-based schematic canvas with drag-and-drop parts,
 wire drawing with pin snapping, and an MNA (modified nodal analysis)
 solver supporting DC operating point, transient and AC sweep analysis.
 Waveforms are shown either as a static plot or as a live oscilloscope,
 and circuits can be saved as .csm JSON or exported as SPICE netlists.
 .
 It is intended as a native replacement for Multisim on Linux.
